,{"accepted_at":"2026-11-26T00:25:16.176279+00:00","exit_code":0,"finished_at":"2026-11-26T00:25:21.624114+00:00","id":"c39125a5ce66b20a8ead","operation":"run_bash","outcome":"completed","target":"CHAD Bash"}],"retention_limit":48,"schema":"GCL_CONTROL_ACTIVITY_FEED/2","transcripts":[{"command":"set -o pipefail; curl -fsS --max-time 10 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grandchallenge/MATHSOLVE/937ae62dba248fee1a43fb107fb36c0c840a3f9e/research/PNP-ABOVE/WP39B_RESULT.md | sed -n '1,24p'","exit_code":0,"id":"ba83ca76b8faa2899576","policy":"GCL_AUTOMATIC_PUBLIC_SOURCE_TRANSCRIPT/1","redactions":{"command":{},"output":{}},"repository":"grandchallenge/MATHSOLVE","revision":"937ae62dba248fee1a43fb107fb36c0c840a3f9e","source_end":"2026-11-26T00:18:00.674892+00:00","stdout_stderr":"# WP39B \u2014 Actual native canonical witness program for the planted family\n\nPinned upstream: `vidick/MIPRE-formalization@5926bdff5db621f44682a101007ef2fe3ae8d970`, Lean 4.35.0-rc3. WP39A protected merge `ffd5b2d01c80e25604c8044d3245ab0c485c14e4` (PR #1307) is the exact source predecessor; all six admitted blobs match the replayed candidate.\n\nThe original `Cost.PolyTimeFun Fml BitStr` program first computes WP35's support list and then maps the native binary equality-to-zero program over it. There is no SAT invocation, search tree, enumeration of the ambient identifier interval, or nonuniform advice. The same total program works for every q, root, and list of planted constraints on the unpinned branch. `witnessProgram_runs` supplies the original encoded execution and polynomial runtime certificate for every input formula, including off-family inputs.\n\n`native_active_model_unique` verifies that every satisfying assignment of the full planted native formula agrees with the explicit planted assignment on every actual active variable. The proof bounds every occurring natural identifier by N\u00b2, gives the exact inverse range map via quotient and remainder, and applies WP39A's finite-variable unique model theorem. Unused infinite assignment coordinates are not claimed unique. `witnessProgram_canonical` establishes the WP38 canonical witness property for the same program on the full family.\n\nCombining with WP39A: for the full satisfiable family, large semantic width for proving the selector or refuting its false branch coexists with a uniform polynomial-time canonical witness constructor. The non-affinity and one-way RepairLaw hypotheses both hold. The construction refutes a general width-to-unrestricted-witness-time implication under these properties. It does not refute every possible structural lower bound or imply P=NP. The width theorem is relative to the specified premise partition and semantic binary calculus; changing that proof model is not covered.\n\nFourteen theorem declarations in one new module, development Lean compilation passed. Exact fresh new-module replay against nine WP39A and 99 WP38B retained source-matched predecessor objects plus standard-axiom audit, protected checks and merge/readback are separate gates. This is internal mathematical verification, not independent certification. The unrestricted lower bound remains open.\n"}],"withheld_candidates":0}
